MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Encore feels like a natural next choice because Broadway songs and vocal collaborations connect directly to my enjoyment of Stages and A Musical Affair.",
    "Partners fits my interest in expressive voices singing together, while Frankie Valli appeals to the nostalgic, melodic side of my listening reflected in The Bang Years."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Greatest Hits: Walking To New Orleans does not connect as strongly to the theatrical vocals and orchestral arrangements I want right now; being older music is not enough to make it a priority.",
    "I cannot confidently connect Very Best of, Hope, or Impressions to my taste from their titles alone. My hesitation reflects uncertainty about the music, rather than a definite dislike."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some older melodic pop seems to have been extended too broadly to greatest-hits collections, even though I prefer Frankie Valli over the other nostalgic choices here.",
    "A romantic or emotional theme offers some appeal, but that alone does not make Love Is Here To Stay or 25 as compelling as Broadway songs and vocal collaborations."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection among Stages, A Musical Affair, and my other vocal selections matters because of the expressive singing and theatrical arrangements, not simply because they are familiar songs.",
    "My latest choice of relaxing classical music suggests that calm, orchestral listening also matters now, alongside my interest in prominent voices."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices capture my interest in expressive vocals and nostalgic melodies, but give too much weight to broad familiarity and too little to theatrical arrangements and relaxing orchestral music."
}
